   ## 7. Grant Sudo Permissions for Specific Commands

   ### Edit sudoers safely
   ```bash
   # Edit main sudoers file
   sudo visudo

   anahur ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL
   # Create specific sudoers file
   sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/john
   ```

   ### Examples of sudo configurations

   #### Allow specific command without password

   ```bash
   sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/custom

   Cmnd_Alias COMMANDS = /usr/sbin/adduser,



   user2 ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: COMMANDS
   ```


   ### Test sudo permissions
   ```bash
   # List user's sudo permissions
   sudo -l

   # Test specific command
   sudo /bin/systemctl status apache2
   ```

   ## 8. Lock and Unlock Users

   ### Lock user account
   ```bash
   # Lock user (prevent login)
   sudo usermod -L john

   # Lock with expiry date
   sudo usermod -e 2025-01-01 john

   # Disable account (alternative method)
   sudo passwd -l john
   ```

   ### Unlock user account
   ```bash
   # Unlock user
   sudo usermod -U john

   # Remove expiry date
   sudo usermod -e "" john

   # Enable account
   sudo passwd -u john
   ```

   ### Check account status
   ```bash
   # Check if account is locked
   sudo passwd -S john

   # View account details
   sudo chage -l john

   # Check login status
   lastlog -u john
   ```

   ## 9. Delete Users

   ### Delete user using deluser (recommended with adduser)
   ```bash
   # Delete user (keep home directory)
   sudo deluser john

   # Delete user and home directory
   sudo deluser --remove-home john

   # Delete user, home, and all files
   sudo deluser --remove-all-files john

   # Force delete (even if logged in)
   sudo deluser --force john
   ```

   ### Alternative deletion methods
   ```bash
   # Using userdel command
   sudo userdel john
   sudo userdel -r john  # with home directory
   ```

   ## 10. Switch Users

   ### Switch to another user
   ```bash
   # Switch with login shell
   su - john

   # Switch without login shell
   su john

   # Switch using sudo (if permitted)
   sudo su - john

   # Execute single command as another user
   sudo -u john whoami
   ```

   ## 11. Complete Example

   ```bash
   # 1. Create user with adduser (interactive)
   sudo adduser webdev

   # 2. Create groups
   sudo addgroup web-developers
   sudo addgroup docker-users

   # 3. Add user to groups
   sudo adduser webdev web-developers
   sudo adduser webdev docker-users
   sudo adduser webdev sudo

   # 4. Create project directory
   sudo mkdir -p /var/www/projects
   sudo chown root:web-developers /var/www/projects
   sudo chmod 2775 /var/www/projects ## we add 2

   # 5. Set up sudo permissions
   sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/webdev
   ```

   Content for `/etc/sudoers.d/webdev`:
   ```bash
   # Web development commands
   Cmnd_Alias WEB_CMDS = /bin/systemctl start nginx, /bin/systemctl stop nginx, /bin/systemctl restart nginx, /bin/systemctl reload nginx
   Cmnd_Alias DOCKER_CMDS = /usr/bin/docker, /usr/local/bin/docker-compose

   webdev ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: WEB_CMDS, DOCKER_CMDS
   ```

